WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.454
User-generated content includes comments, profiles, tickets, documentation
fields, CMS content, product descriptions, knowledge-base articles, and
other text that people or external systems can influence.

2
00:00:12.454 --> 00:00:17.201
Some applications need only plain text, which should usually be rendered
as text.

3
00:00:17.201 --> 00:00:21.261
Others need markdown, limited formatting, links, or richer content.

4
00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:28.348
The first security decision is the content policy: what formatting is
allowed, for whom, and in which rendering contexts.

5
00:00:28.348 --> 00:00:34.196
Sanitization at a high level means preserving approved formatting while
removing unsafe behavior.

6
00:00:34.196 --> 00:00:39.701
It should rely on vetted libraries and clear allowlists rather than ad hoc
string replacement.

7
00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:47.957
Browser parsing is complicated, and simple replacement rules tend to miss
malformed input, encoded forms, context changes, or new features.

8
00:00:47.957 --> 00:00:54.975
A maintainable policy defines allowed elements, allowed attributes, URL
rules, and where sanitized output may be used.

9
00:00:54.975 --> 00:00:58.553
Storing raw versus sanitized content is a real design choice.

10
00:00:58.553 --> 00:01:03.783
Raw content can be reprocessed if the policy changes, but it must not be
casually rendered.

11
00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:09.081
Sanitized content can simplify display, but policy changes may require re-
sanitization.

12
00:01:09.081 --> 00:01:11.970
Some systems store both with strict access rules.

13
00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:18.989
Whatever the choice, teams need to know which version is shown in
templates, emails, previews, exports, and admin views.

14
00:01:18.989 --> 00:01:23.117
Rich content also needs ownership, moderation, and lifecycle review.

15
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:28.208
A markdown feature added for internal documentation may later be exposed
to customers.

16
00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:32.062
A product description field may later appear in an email campaign.

17
00:01:32.062 --> 00:01:35.571
A support ticket may later be rendered in an admin dashboard.

18
00:01:35.571 --> 00:01:42.520
Secure rendering treats rich content as a continuing trust boundary, not a
one-time cleanup at the moment data is saved.
